From c99867001e217f70447dab363a7341041131e227 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 00:37:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] P3-printing-module-repositories

Printing Module, Phase 3 (Infrastructure: repository implementations + IUnitOfWork wiring):

- PrinterRepo: GetPagedAsync (tri-state IsDeleted, type/branch filters), GetByIdIncludingDeletedAsync,
  UniqueNumberExistsAsync - mirrors ProductRepo/BranchRepo exactly
- MaticaPrinterConfigRepo: GetByPrinterIdAsync, GetByPrinterIdsAsync bulk-dictionary load
  (mirrors StockRepo.GetManyForUpdateAsync's shape) - backs list pagination without N+1
- RibbonTypeRepo: ExistsAsync only (GetAllAsync inherited from GenericRepo - global,
  non-tenant-scoped reference table)
- MaticaProductPrintConfigRepo / EvolisProductPrintConfigRepo: GetByProductIdAsync (no
  tracking, reads) + GetByProductIdForUpdateAsync (tracked, for IProductPrintConfigComposer's
  update-in-place or Q-08 hard-delete-on-switch)
- PrintImageRepo: GetByOriginalFileNameAsync, tracked (Q-10's replace flow removes the row directly)

IUnitOfWork / UnitOfWork: six new repo properties (Printers, MaticaPrinterConfigs, RibbonTypes,
MaticaProductPrintConfigs, EvolisProductPrintConfigs, PrintImages), instantiated in the
constructor alongside the existing ones. Property names verified 1:1 between interface and
implementation (17/17 match).

Verified (no dotnet SDK in this sandbox, so no compile - see the same caveat as P1):
brace/paren balance on every touched file, and that every LINQ/EF-async method call has a
corresponding using directive (System.Linq only where Where/OrderBy/Skip/Take/ToDictionary/
Contains are actually used; EF's own async terminal operators - FirstOrDefaultAsync, AnyAsync,
ToListAsync, CountAsync, IgnoreQueryFilters - don't need it and the four leanest repos
correctly omit it).
